The [machine verification record](../reference/ha-coverage-verification.json) preserves source review, independent review, automated checks and publication evidence separately. Failed checks require correction and a recorded rerun. Do not mark a native or assistive-technology check as passed because its documentation example passes.

## Maintain the result

On a Home Assistant upgrade, extract the same registries again and compare additions, removals and aliases. Recheck the official writing and design sources when their content changes. Review the affected guidance and terms before updating hashes or denominators. Check each changed example in the browser and preserve its published address or document a migration.

When a third-party component introduces a new interaction, record its source, capability, styling hooks and failure states before assigning it to an existing family. A native fallback is an honest boundary; it is not evidence of a finished custom implementation.
